<title>POLAND: NBP sells PLN 571 mln of 91-day bills.</title>
<headline>NBP sells PLN 571 mln of 91-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland sold 571 million zlotys worth of its 91-day bills at a tender for money market dealers on demand of the same size against a 800 million zloty offer, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The average yield of the 91-day paper eased to 22.13 percent form 22.19 percent at the last tender on April 17.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
